{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a7481cf9-cad5-44e3-9966-7cadb5e99ee4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a66d14a138280e8c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-3g4mugyz/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E001.md","content":"# GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: the full inventory of gaps\nbetween current Llama Stack Tech Preview quality and the GA bar. It produces\nthe definitive GA scope that all downstream GA work is planned against. The\nassessment consolidates scattered TP feedback (support tickets, known issues)\nand systematically evaluates the four gap dimensions named by the strategy:\nAPI stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate and triage TP feedback from support tickets and other feedback\n  channels into a single deduplicated inventory.\n- Audit the published API surface (OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n  LlamaStackDistribution CRD) for stability gaps: unversioned or\n  churn-prone endpoints, undocumented behaviors, breaking changes across\n  recent TP releases.\n- Assess upgrade paths: what is required to upgrade from the last two TP\n  releases, including whether upgrade-test infrastructure exists.\n- Assess scale limits: current known ceilings (concurrent distributions,\n  request throughput, resource footprint) versus GA expectations.\n- Assess error handling: failure modes, error surfaced to users, retry and\n  degradation behavior.\n- For each gap, classify it as must-fix-for-GA vs. deferrable, and map it to\n  the owning workstream (API stability hardening, support posture, TrustyAI\n  guardrails integration, Dashboard enablement).\n- Produce a GA scope document defining the definitive GA scope, and obtain\n  stakeholder acceptance of it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A GA-readiness gap inventory exists covering all four named dimensions\n  (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with every\n  gap classified as must-fix-for-GA or deferrable and mapped to an owning\n  workstream.\n- TP feedback from support tickets is triaged and reflected in the inventory\n  (no known TP feedback channel left unconsolidated).\n- A GA scope document is produced and accepted by the strategy's\n  stakeholders, defining what is in and out of GA scope.\n- The assessment explicitly states whether upgrade-test infrastructure for\n  the last two TP releases exists, and what is needed if not.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current\n  TP quality and GA bar, producing the definitive GA scope — this epic is\n  the direct delivery of HLR-1.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This investigation gates all implementation workstreams in this strategy\n  (API stability, support posture, guardrails integration, Dashboard\n  enablement): the strategy's Open Question 1 states the size of the\n  stability and hardening work is an estimate until this assessment lands.\n  Downstream epics carry a rewrite gate against it.\n- The outcome space is an unbounded gap inventory (not a small bounded set\n  of alternatives), so downstream work is gated and phased rather than\n  split into conditional branch epics.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35522,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a628f8365d64072b","agent_id":"abd6aadf590dfc4cd","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"bb0ce9b4-0879-4c72-bb22-196215cda056","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:18:27.992Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
