 feasible).\n- All API-stability gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by the GA-readiness\n  assessment are remediated or explicitly deferred with stakeholder\n  sign-off recorded in the assessment's scope document.\n- The stability guarantee statement is published alongside the GA API\n  surface.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): Published API surface carries a stability guarantee —\n  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the\n  last two TP releases. This epic is the direct delivery of HLR-2.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: the definitive set of\n  must-fix stability gaps (and the state of upgrade-test infrastructure)\n  is determined by that assessment; if it finds the hardening work larger\n  or smaller than estimated, this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36352,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a628f8365d64072b","agent_id":"abd6aadf590dfc4cd","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"64ea88e2-0086-49f5-90ad-6b2f62d22e84","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:18:39.105Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
