xplicitly deferred with\n  stakeholder sign-off recorded in the assessment's scope document.\n- The support posture documentation is reviewed and accepted by the\n  stakeholders who own support commitments.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P0): Production support posture is in place — documented SLO\n  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. This epic\n  is the direct delivery of HLR-3.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: the supported\n  configuration matrix and any hardening required to meet SLO targets\n  follow from the assessment's gap inventory; if it changes the GA scope,\n  this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n- SLO and backport commitments require human approval (support/product\n  sign-off) as an explicit part of the deliverable.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37057,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a628f8365d64072b","agent_id":"abd6aadf590dfc4cd","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"146c75a6-95c1-4ae5-9580-5267f6aef5bb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:18:49.925Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
