upported Llama Stack\n  distribution integration, and a validation evidence report is produced.\n- Every failure found is triaged (TrustyAI-side defect, distribution-side\n  defect, or documentation gap), with must-fix-for-GA items resolved or\n  explicitly deferred with stakeholder sign-off.\n- The TrustyAI team confirms (or qualifies, with documented limitations)\n  that TrustyAI guardrails are supported as a backend for Llama Stack GA\n  distributions.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P1): Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n  integration for GA distributions. This epic delivers the TrustyAI-team\n  validation half of HLR-4; the distribution-side integration work is\n  tracked separately by the RHOAI GenAI team.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This epic is the passive-component exception applied to TrustyAI: the\n  strategy lists TrustyAI as affected, and because a different team\n  (TrustyAI) validates that component, the validation is a separate\n  Implementation epic owned by that team rather than an acceptance\n  criterion on the distribution-side epic.\n- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment, and the validation runs\n  against the delivered distribution-side integration, so it is serial\n  after both.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38522,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a628f8365d64072b","agent_id":"abd6aadf590dfc4cd","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"6be010e5-c366-40a9-a32d-3d8429577da8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:19:14.372Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
