readiness assessment remediated or explicitly deferred with\n  stakeholder sign-off.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). This epic is the direct delivery\n  of HLR-5.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: whether default\n  enablement is safe as-is or blocked by must-fix gaps is an assessment\n  outcome; if blockers exist, this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n- The point at which the default flip ships relative to the other GA\n  workstreams is a release-coordination decision (default enablement\n  should land with GA), not a build dependency — the Dashboard change\n  builds against no artifact from the other workstreams.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39313,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a628f8365d64072b","agent_id":"abd6aadf590dfc4cd","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"9f50f098-6c2c-4a1f-a9b3-bd344008e50b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:19:25.941Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
