 with TrustyAI (supported integration)\n  6. Support posture: SLOs, backports, support boundaries\n  7. Troubleshooting and known limitations from the GA-readiness assessment\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The Llama Stack documentation set reflects GA status: no TP-status\n  caveats remain on GA-supported capabilities, and remaining limitations\n  are accurately stated.\n- Migration notes from TP exist, covering the upgrade path from the last\n  two TP releases, deprecated APIs and their replacements, and required\n  configuration changes.\n- The supported TrustyAI guardrails integration, support posture, and\n  default Dashboard experience are documented.\n- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented GA\n  behavior (reviewed by engineers familiar with the delivered work), with\n  review sign-off recorded.\n- Documentation builds and publishes through the standard docs content\n  pipeline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P2): Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including\n  migration notes from TP. This epic is the direct delivery of HLR-6.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This epic is blocked by all implementation workstreams in this strategy:\n  documentation describes what was built, so it runs last.\n- Priority derives from the strategy's `priority: Critical` frontmatter\n  per the docs-authoring priority exception (Critical → P0), not from\n  HLR-6's P2 label.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39996,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a628f8365d64072b","agent_id":"abd6aadf590dfc4cd","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"056449f1-426c-43be-9f93-0532cdc38d69","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:19:37.875Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
