rails integration needs GA-bar remediation (vs. promotion as-is) is an assessment outcome. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n77\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 | The TrustyAI-side validation scope follows the assessment's determination of the guardrails integration's GA readiness. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n78\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Default enablement for entitled clusters presumes GA-bar readiness; the assessment determines whether blockers exist that change the enablement scope. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n79\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 13 (consumer of artifact) | The TrustyAI team's end-to-end validation verifies the supported integration delivered by the Llama Stack distribution work; the validation consumes that integration as its test subject, so it is serial after it. |\n80\t| E002 → E007 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by all Implementation epics; docs describe what was built, including the versioned API surface and upgrade path. |\n81\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same — migration and support documentation reflects the delivered support posture. |\n82\t| E004 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same — the supported guardrails integration must be documented as supported. |\n83\t| E005 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same — validation outcomes (supported configurations, limitations) feed the documentation. |\n84\t| E006 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same — docs describe the default Dashboard experience. |\n85\t\n86\tNon-edges (deliberate):\n87\t- E002 ∥ E003 (Rule 15): same component and team but distinct logical changes\n88\t  (API hardening engineering vs. support policy definition); no shared\n89\t  artifact — parallel.\n90\t- E002/E003 ∥ E004/E006 (Rule 14): independent work areas, no shared\n91\t  build-against artifacts — parallel.\n92\t- No edge from E002/E003 to E006: the timing of flipping the Dashboard\n93\t  default is a release-coordination decision, not a build dependency; the\n94\t  Dashboard change does not build against the API-stability artifacts.\n95\t\n96\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n97\t\n98\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n99\t|-----|----------|---------|\n100\t| HLR-1 (GA-readiness assessment) | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 |\n101\t| HLR-2 (API stability guarantee) | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 |\n102\t| HLR-3 (production support posture) | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 |\n103\t| HLR-4 (TrustyAI guardrails supported integration) | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E004, RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 |\n104\t| HLR-5 (Dashboard default enablement) | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 |\n105\t| HLR-6 (GA documentation uplift) | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E007 |\n106\t\n107\tAll six HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n108\t\n109\t## Component Mapping Notes\n110\t\n111\t- All components are canonical names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`\n112\t  (Llama Stack, TrustyAI, Dashboard, Documentation) — no non-obvious mappings.\n113\t- E004's work spans Llama Stack (the distribution that promotes the\n114\t  integration from experimental flag to supported) and TrustyAI (the backend);\n115\t  the single most-relevant canonical component is **Llama Stack**, owned by\n116\t  RHOAI GenAI. The TrustyAI-side validation is a separate epic (E005)\n117\t  because a different team (TrustyAI) validates that component — the\n118\t  passive-component exception in Step 2.\n119\t- E007 uses canonical component **Documentation**. No architecture context\n120\t  file exists for Documentation; owning team assigned as RHOAI GenAI (the\n121\t  component graduating to GA) — see Health Warnings.\n122\t\n123\t## Health Warnings\n124\t\n125\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy provides only a bullet list of\n126\t  affected components (no owner-team or change detail), and has no Impacted\n127\t  Teams table, Dependencies table, acceptance criteria (Given/When/Then), or\n128\t  NFRs. Teams were derived from `.context/architecture-context/` owning teams\n129\t  (RHOAI GenAI, TrustyAI, RHOAI Dashboard). Owners should confirm.\n130\t- **Priority inversion flag (informational)**: HLR-6 is P2 in the strategy,\n131\t  but the docs-authoring epic derives P0 from the strategy's `priority:\n132\t  Critical` frontmatter per the docs-authoring priority exception. This is\n133\t  rule-compliant, not an error, but reviewers should be aware the HLR label\n134\t  and the epic priority intentionally differ.\n135\t- **Scope trap (mild)**: HLR-2's \"tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n136\t  releases\" implies upgrade-test infrastructure whose existence is not\n137\t  confirmed in the strategy. It is captured as an acceptance criterion on\n138\t  E002 rather than a separate epic; if the assessment (E001) finds no such\n139\t  infrastructure exists, that epic's scope rewrites accordingly.\n140\t- **Open Question 1** (GA scope unknown until assessment) is modeled as the\n141\t  E001 investigation gating all implementation epics with `rewrite` impact —\n142\t  not a bounded set of outcomes, so no conditional branch epics were created;\n143\t  this is a gated/phased decomposition.\n144\t\n145\t## Tiered Delivery\n146\t\n147\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing; the\n148\tonly gate is the internal GA-readiness assessment, modeled as a blocking\n149\tInvestigation (E001) rather than a tiered delivery split. Partial value\n150\tbefore E001 lands is not meaningful because E001 defines the GA scope itself.\n151\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30541914ce9fc3f","agent_id":"adc87dcd8807cc83a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"78f30d0f-34b3-4197-83f2-6e2befd30b3d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:22:02.122Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f4ac35081a50fe3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
