esource footprint) versus GA expectations.\n48\t- Assess error handling: failure modes, error surfaced to users, retry and\n49\t  degradation behavior.\n50\t- For each gap, classify it as must-fix-for-GA vs. deferrable, and map it to\n51\t  the owning workstream (API stability hardening, support posture, TrustyAI\n52\t  guardrails integration, Dashboard enablement).\n53\t- Produce a GA scope document defining the definitive GA scope, and obtain\n54\t  stakeholder acceptance of it.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A GA-readiness gap inventory exists covering all four named dimensions\n59\t  (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with every\n60\t  gap classified as must-fix-for-GA or deferrable and mapped to an owning\n61\t  workstream.\n62\t- TP feedback from support tickets is triaged and reflected in the inventory\n63\t  (no known TP feedback channel left unconsolidated).\n64\t- A GA scope document is produced and accepted by the strategy's\n65\t  stakeholders, defining what is in and out of GA scope.\n66\t- The assessment explicitly states whether upgrade-test infrastructure for\n67\t  the last two TP releases exists, and what is needed if not.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P0): GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current\n72\t  TP quality and GA bar, producing the definitive GA scope — this epic is\n73\t  the direct delivery of HLR-1.\n74\t\n75\t## Notes\n76\t\n77\t- This investigation gates all implementation workstreams in this strategy\n78\t  (API stability, support posture, guardrails integration, Dashboard\n79\t  enablement): the strategy's Open Question 1 states the size of the\n80\t  stability and hardening work is an estimate until this assessment lands.\n81\t  Downstream epics carry a rewrite gate against it.\n82\t- The outcome space is an unbounded gap inventory (not a small bounded set\n83\t  of alternatives), so downstream work is gated and phased rather than\n84\t  split into conditional branch epics.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30541914ce9fc3f","agent_id":"adc87dcd8807cc83a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"35ad294f-c091-41a1-8789-8e6991db5b46","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:22:05.017Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd0343dac58f1b3b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
