anges are versioned,\n50\t  how deprecations are announced, and how long deprecated surfaces remain\n51\t  supported.\n52\t- Remediate API-stability gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by the\n53\t  GA-readiness assessment.\n54\t- Build and execute upgrade-path tests from the last two TP releases to the\n55\t  GA release (including whatever upgrade-test infrastructure proves\n56\t  necessary), producing repeatable evidence.\n57\t- Publish the stability guarantee statement for the GA API surface.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- The published API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme is\n62\t  documented.\n63\t- A deprecation policy is documented and consistently applied: any TP API\n64\t  surface not carried into GA is either preserved per policy or explicitly\n65\t  deprecated with a migration path.\n66\t- A tested upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases to the GA\n67\t  release exists, with repeatable test evidence (automated where feasible).\n68\t- All API-stability gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by the GA-readiness\n69\t  assessment are remediated or explicitly deferred with stakeholder\n70\t  sign-off recorded in the assessment's scope document.\n71\t- The stability guarantee statement is published alongside the GA API\n72\t  surface.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-2 (P0): Published API surface carries a stability guarantee —\n77\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the\n78\t  last two TP releases. This epic is the direct delivery of HLR-2.\n79\t\n80\t## Notes\n81\t\n82\t- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: the definitive set of\n83\t  must-fix stability gaps (and the state of upgrade-test infrastructure)\n84\t  is determined by that assessment; if it finds the hardening work larger\n85\t  or smaller than estimated, this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30541914ce9fc3f","agent_id":"adc87dcd8807cc83a","session_i