ion matrix relevant to\n51\t  the integration.\n52\t- Validate the TrustyAI-side integration points the Llama Stack safety\n53\t  provider relies on (service provisioning per data science project,\n54\t  guardrail API behavior, failure and error propagation).\n55\t- Record validation evidence: pass/fail per scenario, reproductions for any\n56\t  failure, and an assessment of whether each failure is a TrustyAI-side\n57\t  defect, a distribution-side defect, or a documentation gap.\n58\t- Surface discovered TrustyAI-side gaps with severity classification, and\n59\t  either resolve in-scope (if must-fix-for-GA per the GA-readiness\n60\t  assessment) or document as known limitations.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- A validation plan exists covering the integration scenarios relevant to\n65\t  the supported configuration matrix, with defined pass/fail criteria per\n66\t  scenario.\n67\t- End-to-end validation is executed against the supported Llama Stack\n68\t  distribution integration, and a validation evidence report is produced.\n69\t- Every failure found is triaged (TrustyAI-side defect, distribution-side\n70\t  defect, or documentation gap), with must-fix-for-GA items resolved or\n71\t  explicitly deferred with stakeholder sign-off.\n72\t- The TrustyAI team confirms (or qualifies, with documented limitations)\n73\t  that TrustyAI guardrails are supported as a backend for Llama Stack GA\n74\t  distributions.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-4 (P1): Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n79\t  integration for GA distributions. This epic delivers the TrustyAI-team\n80\t  validation half of HLR-4; the distribution-side integration work is\n81\t  tracked separately by the RHOAI GenAI team.\n82\t\n83\t## Notes\n84\t\n85\t- This epic is the passive-component exception applied to TrustyAI: the\n86\t  strategy lists TrustyAI as affected, and because a different team\n87\t  (TrustyAI) validates that component, the validation is a separate\n88\t  Implementation epic owned by that team rather than an acceptance\n89\t  criterion on the distribution-side epic.\n90\t- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment, and the validation runs\n91\t  against the delivered distribution-side integration, so it is serial\n92\t  after both.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30541914ce9fc3f","agent_id":"adc87dcd8807cc83a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"ac86f655-6c69-4a32-93a3-f8e5a3e7db2c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:22:13.920Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f414038c139a4d0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
