t  re-enabled by the default change.\n51\t- Verify the default Llama Stack management experience (navigation,\n52\t  resource views, and status surfaces the Dashboard already ships) works\n53\t  without the opt-in gate against a GA Llama Stack distribution.\n54\t- Remediate Dashboard-side gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by the\n55\t  GA-readiness assessment.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- On an entitled cluster with no explicit opt-in or opt-out configuration,\n60\t  Llama Stack management is enabled in the Dashboard by default.\n61\t- The TP opt-in gate no longer controls Llama Stack management visibility\n62\t  for entitled clusters.\n63\t- Clusters without entitlement, and clusters with an explicit disable\n64\t  configuration, show unchanged behavior.\n65\t- The default-enabled experience is verified against a GA-configured\n66\t  Llama Stack distribution, with any Dashboard-side must-fix gaps from the\n67\t  GA-readiness assessment remediated or explicitly deferred with\n68\t  stakeholder sign-off.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-5 (P1): The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n73\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). This epic is the direct delivery\n74\t  of HLR-5.\n75\t\n76\t## Notes\n77\t\n78\t- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: whether default\n79\t  enablement is safe as-is or blocked by must-fix gaps is an assessment\n80\t  outcome; if blockers exist, this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n81\t- The point at which the default flip ships relative to the other GA\n82\t  workstreams is a release-coordination decision (default enablement\n83\t  should land with GA), not a build dependency — the Dashboard change\n84\t  builds against no artifact from the other workstreams.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85b5de9eb80b712","agent_id":"afa05c7d191f9514a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"0f4e2cbf-e310-4dff-91cb-51ca017b8e98","timestamp":"2026-10