{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b73853a243801ad4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-9014 — Graduate Llama Stack to General Availability\n11\t\n12\tStrategy: RHAISTRAT-9014 (Critical, Refinement Done). Llama Stack is Tech\n13\tPreview with strong adoption; GA graduation requires closing quality gaps\n14\twhose full inventory is not yet known (HLR-1), then delivering API stability\n15\t(HLR-2), a production support posture (HLR-3), a supported TrustyAI guardrails\n16\tintegration (HLR-4), Dashboard default enablement (HLR-5), and GA-standard\n17\tdocumentation (HLR-6).\n18\t\n19\t**Triage (Step 0):** Not below-threshold — the strategy spans three components\n20\towned by three distinct teams (Llama Stack / TrustyAI / Dashboard per\n21\tarchitecture context) and contains a genuine unknown (Open Question 1: the GA\n22\tscope itself is unknown until the HLR-1 assessment lands). Not documentation\n23\tonly — substantive code, integration, and configuration work is required.\n24\t\n25\t## Epic List\n26\t\n27\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n28\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 | GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 | Llama Stack API stability guarantees and tested upgrade path | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 | Llama Stack production support posture | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E004 | Supported TrustyAI guardrails integration in Llama Stack GA distributions | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P1 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 | TrustyAI-side validation of the guardrails integration with Llama Stack | Implementation | TrustyAI | P1 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 | Dashboard default enablement of Llama Stack management for entitled clusters | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E007 | Llama Stack GA documentation uplift and TP migration notes | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n36\t\n37\tPriorities: E001 is P0 directly (HLR-1) and blocks all P0 implementation work.\n38\tE002/E003 map to P0 HLRs. E004/E005/E006 map to P1 HLRs. E007 is a\n39\t`docs-authoring` epic — exempt from priority inheritance; its priority derives\n40\tfrom the strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0 per the\n41\tdocs-authoring priority exception.\n42\t\n43\t## Dependency DAG\n44\t\n45\t```mermaid\n46\tgraph TD\n47\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 GA-readiness assessment]\n48\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 API stability]\n49\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 support posture]\n50\t    E004[RHAISTRAT-9014-E004 TrustyAI guardrails integration]\n51\t    E005[RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 TrustyAI validation]\n52\t    E006[RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 Dashboard default enablement]\n53\t    E007[RHAISTRAT-9014-E007 GA documentation]\n54\t\n55\t    E001 --> E002\n56\t    E001 --> E003\n57\t    E001 --> E004\n58\t    E001 --> E005\n59\t    E001 --> E006\n60\t    E004 --> E005\n61\t    E002 --> E007\n62\t    E003 --> E007\n63\t    E004 --> E007\n64\t    E005 --> E007\n65\t    E006 --> E007\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\tCritical path: E001 → E004 → E005 → E007 (length 4).\n69\t\n70\t## DAG Justification\n71\t\n72\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n73\t|------|------|-----------|\n74\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 | The assessment produces the definitive GA scope; the size and content of the API stability and hardening work is explicitly an estimate until it lands (Open Question 1). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n75\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 | The supported configuration matrix and hardening scope for the support posture are determined by the assessment's gap inventory. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n76\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | Whether the TrustyAI guardrails integration needs GA-bar remediation (vs. promotion as-is) is an assessment outcome. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n77\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 | The TrustyAI-side validation scope follows the assessment's determination of the guardrails integration's GA readiness. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n78\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Default enablement for entitled clusters presumes GA-bar readiness; the assessment determines whether blockers exist that change the enablement scope. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n79\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 13 (consumer of artifact) | The TrustyAI team's end-to-end validation verifies the supported integration delivered by the Llama Stack distribution work; the validation consumes that integration as its test subject, so it is serial after it. |\n80\t| E002 → E007 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by all Implementation epics; docs describe what was built, including the versioned API surface and upgrade path. |\n81\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same — migration and support documentation reflects the delivered support posture. |\n82\t| E004 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same — the supported guardrails integration must be documented as supported. |\n83\t| E005 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same — validation outcomes (supported configurations, limitations) feed the documentation. |\n84\t| E006 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same — docs describe the default Dashboard experience. |\n85\t\n86\tNon-edges (deliberate):\n87\t- E002 ∥ E003 (Rule 15): same component and team but distinct logical changes\n88\t  (API hardening engineering vs. support policy definition); no shared\n89\t  artifact — parallel.\n90\t- E002/E003 ∥ E004/E006 (Rule 14): independent work areas, no shared\n91\t  build-against artifacts — parallel.\n92\t- No edge from E002/E003 to E006: the timing of flipping the Dashboard\n93\t  default is a release-coordination decision, not a build dependency; the\n94\t  Dashboard change does not build against the API-stability artifacts,\n95\t  and E006's verification runs against a staged GA-candidate\n96\t  distribution rather than requiring the GA workstreams to be complete\n97\t  (sequencing assumption recorded in E006's Notes).\n98\t\n99\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n100\t\n101\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n102\t|-----|----------|---------|\n103\t| HLR-1 (GA-readiness assessment) | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 |\n104\t| HLR-2 (API stability guarantee) | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 |\n105\t| HLR-3 (production support posture) | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 |\n106\t| HLR-4 (TrustyAI guardrails supported integration) | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E004, RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 |\n107\t| HLR-5 (Dashboard default enablement) | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 |\n108\t| HLR-6 (GA documentation uplift) | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E007 |\n109\t\n110\tAll six HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n111\t\n112\t## Component Mapping Notes\n113\t\n114\t- All components are canonical names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`\n115\t  (Llama Stack, TrustyAI, Dashboard, Documentation) — no non-obvious mappings.\n116\t- E004's work spans Llama Stack (the distribution that promotes the\n117\t  integration from experimental flag to supported) and TrustyAI (the backend);\n118\t  the single most-relevant canonical component is **Llama Stack**, owned by\n119\t  RHOAI GenAI. The TrustyAI-side validation is a separate epic (E005)\n120\t  because a different team (TrustyAI) validates that component — the\n121\t  passive-component exception in Step 2.\n122\t- E007 uses canonical component **Documentation**. No architecture context\n123\t  file exists for Documentation; owning team assigned as RHOAI GenAI (the\n124\t  component graduating to GA) — see Health Warnings.\n125\t- Documentation ownership (revision): the docs-authoring epic (E007) is\n126\t  the sole owner of user-facing documentation authoring for the\n127\t  graduation. The implementation epics deliver normative policy and\n128\t  definition content only — E002 the versioning scheme, deprecation\n129\t  policy, and stability guarantee commitment; E003 the SLO targets,\n130\t  backport policy, and supported configuration matrix; E004 the\n131\t  supported guardrails integration surface — which E007 consumes as\n132\t  input when authoring the user-facing documentation set. No user-facing\n133\t  documentation deliverable is claimed by more than one epic.\n134\t\n135\t## Health Warnings\n136\t\n137\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy provides only a bullet list of\n138\t  affected components (no owner-team or change detail), and has no Impacted\n139\t  Teams table, Dependencies table, acceptance criteria (Given/When/Then), or\n140\t  NFRs. Teams were derived from `.context/architecture-context/` owning teams\n141\t  (RHOAI GenAI, TrustyAI, RHOAI Dashboard). Owners should confirm.\n142\t- **Priority inversion flag (informational)**: HLR-6 is P2 in the strategy,\n143\t  but the docs-authoring epic derives P0 from the strategy's `priority:\n144\t  Critical` frontmatter per the docs-authoring priority exception. This is\n145\t  rule-compliant, not an error, but reviewers should be aware the HLR label\n146\t  and the epic priority intentionally differ.\n147\t- **Scope trap (mild)**: HLR-2's \"tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n148\t  releases\" implies upgrade-test infrastructure whose existence is not\n149\t  confirmed in the strategy. It is captured as an acceptance criterion on\n150\t  E002 rather than a separate epic; if the assessment (E001) finds no such\n151\t  infrastructure exists, that epic's scope rewrites accordingly.\n152\t- **Open Question 1** (GA scope unknown until assessment) is modeled as the\n153\t  E001 investigation gating all implementation epics with `rewrite` impact —\n154\t  not a bounded set of outcomes, so no conditional branch epics were created;\n155\t  this is a gated/phased decomposition.\n156\t\n157\t## Tiered Delivery\n158\t\n159\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing; the\n160\tonly gate is the internal GA-readiness assessment, modeled as a blocking\n161\tInvestigation (E001) rather than a tiered delivery split. Partial value\n162\tbefore E001 lands is not meaningful because E001 defines the GA scope itself.\n163\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ffa35ee02cccdf1","agent_id":"a6bc45ff6df2ae44a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"62c73efa-42ab-4c4f-bd5a-f3dcae2dd23f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:29:46.208Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b73853a243801ad4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
