ion matrix: the provider\n53\t  combinations (e.g., inference and vector providers), deployment sizes,\n54\t  and platform versions that are supported at GA, aligned with the\n55\t  GA-readiness assessment's findings.\n56\t- Remediate support-posture gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by the\n57\t  GA-readiness assessment.\n58\t- Deliver the support posture (SLO targets, backport policy, supported\n59\t  configuration matrix) as normative policy content for the GA\n60\t  documentation workstream, which authors the user-facing support\n61\t  documentation where support and customers consume it.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- SLO targets are defined as normative policy content for the GA\n66\t  distribution, with the measurement approach stated for each target.\n67\t- The backport policy is documented, covering fix scope, supported release\n68\t  trains, and duration.\n69\t- The supported configuration matrix is documented, and every entry is\n70\t  either validated or explicitly marked experimental/unsupported.\n71\t- All support-posture gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by the\n72\t  GA-readiness assessment are remediated or explicitly deferred with\n73\t  stakeholder sign-off recorded in the assessment's scope document.\n74\t- The normative support posture content is reviewed and accepted by the\n75\t  stakeholders who own support commitments; the user-facing support\n76\t  documentation is authored by the GA documentation workstream.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- HLR-3 (P0): Production support posture is in place — documented SLO\n81\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. This epic\n82\t  is the direct delivery of HLR-3.\n83\t\n84\t## Notes\n85\t\n86\t- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: the supported\n87\t  configuration matrix and any hardening required to meet SLO targets\n88\t  follow from the assessment's gap inventory; if it changes the GA scope,\n89\t  this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n90\t- SLO and backport commitments require human approval (support/product\n91\t  sign-off) as an explicit part of the deliverable.\n92\t- Documentation boundary: this epic defines the support posture as\n93\t  normative policy content only. The user-facing support-posture\n94\t  documentation is authored by the GA documentation workstream from this\n95\t  epic's normative output.\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ffa35ee02cccdf1","agent_id":"a6bc45ff6df2ae44a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"9c24719e-41d7-4060-befb-77e646de38d2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:29:52.094Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6aa2bc2d65cd2da","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
