{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2956c2f64b81b39","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: Supported TrustyAI guardrails integration in Llama Stack GA distributions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds the guardrails integration\n15\t    below GA bar, rewrite this epic's scope to include the assessed remediation before\n16\t    promotion from experimental flag.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Supported TrustyAI guardrails integration in Llama Stack GA distributions\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic promotes the TrustyAI safety-guardrails integration in Llama Stack\n39\tfrom an experimental flag to a supported, documented integration in GA\n40\tdistributions. After this epic, users of GA Llama Stack distributions can\n41\tconfigure TrustyAI-backed safety guardrails as a supported capability with\n42\tdocumentation and defined behavior, not an opt-in experiment.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Promote the TrustyAI guardrails integration from experimental flag to a\n47\t  supported configuration in Llama Stack GA distributions, following the\n48\t  promotion mechanism resolved during implementation.\n49\t- Remediate guardrails-integration gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by\n50\t  the GA-readiness assessment (the strategy's problem statement\n51\t  specifically calls out quality gaps that TP status excuses).\n52\t- Define the supported integration surface: which TrustyAI guardrail\n53\t  capabilities are supported through the Llama Stack safety provider\n54\t  interface, its configuration mechanism, and its limitations, recorded\n55\t  as normative engineering input for the GA documentation workstream\n56\t  (the user-facing guardrails documentation is authored there, not in\n57\t  this epic).\n58\t- Coordinate with the TrustyAI team's end-to-end validation of the\n59\t  integration and resolve or document issues it surfaces.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A GA Llama Stack distribution can be configured with TrustyAI safety\n64\t  guardrails without any experimental or TP opt-in flag.\n65\t- The supported integration surface is defined and recorded as normative\n66\t  engineering input — configuration mechanism, supported capabilities,\n67\t  and known limitations — for the GA documentation workstream that\n68\t  authors the user-facing documentation.\n69\t- All guardrails-integration gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by the\n70\t  GA-readiness assessment are remediated or explicitly deferred with\n71\t  stakeholder sign-off recorded in the assessment's scope document.\n72\t- Functional testing of the guardrails integration passes against a\n73\t  TrustyAI service instance in a GA-distribution configuration.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-4 (P1): Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n78\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. This epic\n79\t  is the primary delivery of HLR-4 on the Llama Stack distribution side;\n80\t  the TrustyAI-side validation of the same integration is tracked\n81\t  separately by the TrustyAI team.\n82\t\n83\t## Notes\n84\t\n85\t- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: whether the integration\n86\t  can be promoted as-is or needs GA-bar remediation is an assessment\n87\t  outcome; if the assessment finds the gap larger than estimated, this\n88\t  epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n89\t- This epic's work spans two strategy components (Llama Stack, where the\n90\t  integration is wired and supported, and TrustyAI, the guardrails\n91\t  backend). Llama Stack is the most-relevant canonical component because\n92\t  the change — removing the experimental flag and supporting the\n93\t  integration — lands in the distribution.\n94\t- Documentation boundary: this epic delivers only the distribution-side\n95\t  promotion, remediation, and the normative definition of the supported\n96\t  integration surface. All user-facing guardrails documentation\n97\t  (configuration steps, supported capabilities, limitations) is authored\n98\t  by the GA documentation workstream, which consumes this epic's\n99\t  normative output as input.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ffa35ee02cccdf1","agent_id":"a6bc45ff6df2ae44a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"01760c27-6ab1-401e-b185-77fa000792d0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:29:52.896Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2956c2f64b81b39","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
