t  re-enabled by the default change.\n51\t- Verify the default Llama Stack management experience (navigation,\n52\t  resource views, and status surfaces the Dashboard already ships) works\n53\t  without the opt-in gate against a staged GA-candidate Llama Stack\n54\t  distribution.\n55\t- Remediate Dashboard-side gaps classified as must-fix-for-GA by the\n56\t  GA-readiness assessment.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- On an entitled cluster with no explicit opt-in or opt-out configuration,\n61\t  Llama Stack management is enabled in the Dashboard by default.\n62\t- The TP opt-in gate no longer controls Llama Stack management visibility\n63\t  for entitled clusters.\n64\t- Clusters without entitlement, and clusters with an explicit disable\n65\t  configuration, show unchanged behavior.\n66\t- The default-enabled experience is verified against a staged GA-candidate\n67\t  Llama Stack distribution, with any Dashboard-side must-fix gaps from the\n68\t  GA-readiness assessment remediated or explicitly deferred with\n69\t  stakeholder sign-off.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-5 (P1): The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n74\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). This epic is the direct delivery\n75\t  of HLR-5.\n76\t\n77\t## Notes\n78\t\n79\t- Scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: whether default\n80\t  enablement is safe as-is or blocked by must-fix gaps is an assessment\n81\t  outcome; if blockers exist, this epic's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n82\t- The point at which the default flip ships relative to the other GA\n83\t  workstreams is a release-coordination decision (default enablement\n84\t  should land with GA), not a build dependency — the Dashboard change\n85\t  builds against no artifact from the other workstreams.\n86\t- Sequencing assumption: verification runs against a staged GA-candidate\n87\t  distribution, not a fully shipped GA distribution, so this epic needs\n88\t  no DAG edge to the API-stability or guardrails workstreams. If\n89\t  verification in practice requires a fully GA-configured distribution,\n90\t  that is a release-coordination sequencing constraint, not a scope\n91\t  change to this epic.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ffa35ee02cccdf1","agent_id":"a6bc45ff6df2ae44a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"3a3d4328-606b-4b35-8b3e-ed45424744c3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:29:57.836Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9369c73b4fba66a6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
