t  the deprecation policy, and any configuration changes required by the\n53\t  supported configuration matrix.\n54\t- Document the supported TrustyAI guardrails integration from the user\n55\t  perspective (setup, supported capabilities, limitations).\n56\t- Document the production support posture where users consume it: SLO\n57\t  targets, backport policy, and support boundaries.\n58\t- Content outline (to be finalized against delivered scope):\n59\t  1. Getting started / GA overview for Llama Stack distributions\n60\t  2. Supported configurations and platform requirements\n61\t  3. API reference for the versioned GA surface, including versioning and\n62\t     deprecation policy\n63\t  4. Upgrade and migration guide (last two TP releases → GA)\n64\t  5. Safety guardrails with TrustyAI (supported integration)\n65\t  6. Support posture: SLOs, backports, support boundaries\n66\t  7. Troubleshooting and known limitations from the GA-readiness assessment\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- The Llama Stack documentation set reflects GA status: no TP-status\n71\t  caveats remain on GA-supported capabilities, and remaining limitations\n72\t  are accurately stated.\n73\t- Migration notes from TP exist, covering the upgrade path from the last\n74\t  two TP releases, deprecated APIs and their replacements, and required\n75\t  configuration changes.\n76\t- The supported TrustyAI guardrails integration, support posture, and\n77\t  default Dashboard experience are documented.\n78\t- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented GA\n79\t  behavior (reviewed by engineers familiar with the delivered work), with\n80\t  review sign-off recorded.\n81\t- Documentation builds and publishes through the standard docs content\n82\t  pipeline.\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability\n85\t\n86\t- HLR-6 (P2): Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including\n87\t  migration notes from TP. This epic is the direct delivery of HLR-6.\n88\t\n89\t## Notes\n90\t\n91\t- This epic is blocked by all implementation workstreams in this strategy:\n92\t  documentation describes what was built, so it runs last.\n93\t- This epic is the sole owner of user-facing documentation authoring for\n94\t  the graduation. The implementation workstreams deliver normative\n95\t  policy and definition content only — the deprecation policy and\n96\t  stability guarantee (API stability workstream), the SLO targets,\n97\t  backport policy, and supported configuration matrix (support posture\n98\t  workstream), and the supported guardrails integration surface\n99\t  (distribution-side integration workstream). This epic consumes those\n100\t  normative inputs and authors the user-facing documentation set,\n101\t  including the guardrails setup/capabilities/limitations page.\n102\t- Priority derives from the strategy's `priority: Critical` frontmatter\n103\t  per the docs-authoring priority exception (Critical → P0), not from\n104\t  HLR-6's P2 label.\n105\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ffa35ee02cccdf1","agent_id":"a6bc45ff6df2ae44a","session_id":"7bc7c06b-886c-4c94-b316-537b910a3f9b","uuid":"fabc09b9-1765-41e8-9af5-ebfb7a2378f6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T01:29:58.508Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a7e30da7714c758","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
